# Build-context exclusions for `docker build -f frontend/Dockerfile .`
#
# Docker prefers a `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` next to the Dockerfile over the
# context-root `.dockerignore`. That matters here: the root `.dockerignore`
# excludes `frontend/` (it is written for the backend image build), and the
# frontend build context IS the repository root — so without this file the
# `COPY frontend/ ...` step would find nothing.
#
# Keep in sync with the root `.dockerignore` for the entries that overlap.

.git
.github
.vscode

# The frontend context needs `frontend/` only; native assets are self-contained.
backend
docs
scripts
vendor
skills
data_agent_app
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/*.pyc

# Never ship installed deps or build output; the image builds them itself.
**/node_modules
**/dist
